## Anti-patterns (do not do)

- **Don't reference Sahil's employer or current work** (see the CRITICAL section at the top). No `we`, `our team`, `this sprint`, `operator tablet`, product surfaces, internal tools, customer numbers. Reframe as past-personal, hypothetical, or teaching.
- Don't write Markdown bold (`**…**`), italics (`*…*`), or backtick-wrapped `code` inside post / comment / connect files. LinkedIn renders them literally. Use Unicode bold/italic (see §3 above) and plain text for code identifiers.
- Don't suggest running `python …` for the daily workflow — there are no automation scripts in this repo anymore. A one-off Python invocation for text conversion (e.g. via the Shell tool) is fine.
- Don't reference `data/comment-targets.csv` or `data/connect-queue.csv` — those files were removed.
- Don't fabricate LinkedIn post URLs or profile URLs.
- Don't write generic LinkedIn AI-sounding posts. If it could be anyone's, rewrite.
